# Week 1 - Python Fundamentals

## Overview

During Week 1, I learned and practiced the fundamental concepts of Python programming through different coding exercises.

## Topics Learned

### Day 1 - Python Basics
- Variables and data types
- Input and output
- If-else conditions
- Loops
- Functions
- Number classification
- Even and odd numbers
- Simple calculator

### Day 2 - Lists and Loops
- Creating and modifying lists
- append(), insert(), remove(), sort(), and reverse()
- Finding maximum and minimum values using loops
- Calculating sum and average
- Creating multiplication tables

### Day 3 - Strings and Dictionaries
- String operations
- Uppercase and lowercase conversion
- Reversing strings
- Counting vowels
- Checking palindromes
- Counting words
- Character frequency using dictionaries

### Day 4 - Functions and Loop Practice
- Creating and calling functions
- Square and cube calculations
- Factorial
- Simple interest
- Prime number checking
- Fibonacci series
- Nested loops
- Pattern printing

### Day 5 - File Handling and Review
- Reading text files
- Writing to text files
- Appending data to files
- Using safe file handling
- Working with dictionaries
- Calculating student averages and grades
- Combining previously learned Python concepts

## Week 1 Summary

Week 1 helped me build a strong foundation in Python. I practiced variables, conditions, loops, functions, lists, strings, dictionaries, and file handling. I also solved several small programming problems that helped me combine these concepts into complete Python programs.
